 splutter","step_8":"Pour tempering over the avial","step_9":"Serve hot with rice"}
{"_id":"d16e91a7-ac6b-44ee-a92f-e24d9fae66c7","number":39,"title":"MEAT BORSCHT","cuisine":"Ukrainian","meal_type":"Soup","preparation_difficulty":"Medium/Hard","preparation_time":"2 hours 30 mins","servings":"8-10","image_source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/P-H-V/FEMIA-images/main/recipe-images/1789339530579_MEAT-BORSCHT.png","source":"Traditional Ukrainian recipe","validation":"USDA - beef provides iron (2.5mg/150g), protein (25g); beets provide folate (136mcg/cup), betalains; cabbage provides vitamin C","confidence":"Supported","tag_1":"menstrual-phase-week-1","tag_2":"fertility-supporting","tag_3":"pregnancy-month-1-3","tag_4":"gluten-free","tag_5":"contains-meat","tag_6":"vitamin-c","tag_7":"iron","tag_8":"iron-rich","tag_9":"antioxidant-rich","tag_10":"fiber","tag_11":"folate","tag_12":"folate-rich","tag_13":"protein","tag_14":"NONE","tag_15":"NONE","principal_ingredient_1":"Beef or pork on the bone","principal_ingredient_2":"beets","principal_ingredient_3":"cabbage","principal_ingredient_4":"potatoes","principal_ingredient_5":"carrots","principal_ingredient_6":"onions","principal_ingredient_7":"tomatoes","subtitle":"Borshch z Miasom","freeRecipe":false,"ingredient_1":"500g beef (chuck or brisket) on the bone, or pork ribs","ingredient_2":"3 medium beets, peeled and julienned","ingredient_3":"1/2 head cabbage, shredded","ingredient_4":"4 medium potatoes, peeled and cubed","ingredient_5":"2 carrots, julienned","ingredient_6":"1 large onion, finely chopped","ingredient_7":"2 tomatoes, grated (or 2 tbsp tomato paste)","ingredient_8":"1 red bell pepper, diced (optional)","ingredient_9":"4 cloves garlic, minced","ingredient_10":"1 bay leaf","ingredient_11":"5 black peppercorns","ingredient_12":"2 tbsp vinegar or lemon juice (to preserve beet color)","ingredient_13":"1 tbsp sugar or honey","ingredient_14":"3 tbsp sunflower oil","ingredient_15":"10 cups cold water","ingredient_16":"Salt to taste","ingredient_17":"Fresh dill for garnish","ingredient_18":"Fresh parsley for garnish","ingredient_19":"Sour cream for serving","step_1":"Place meat in a large pot with cold water, bring to a boil. Skim off foam thoroughly","step_2":"Reduce heat to low, add bay leaf and peppercorns, and simmer for 1.5 hours until meat is tender and falling off the bone","step_3":"Remove meat, shred or cut into bite-sized pieces, return to broth","step_4":"In a separate large pan, heat oil and sauté beets for 3-4 minutes","step_5":"Add vinegar and sugar to beets (preserves color), cook for 2 more minutes","step_6":"Add onions and carrots to beets, cook for 5 minutes until softened","step_7":"Add bell pepper (if using) and grated tomatoes, cook for 3 minutes","step_8":"Transfer sautéed vegetables to the broth","step_9":"Add potatoes and cabbage, bring to a boil","step_10":"Reduce heat and simmer for 20-25 minutes until all vegetables are tender","step_11":"Add minced garlic, salt, and pepper in the last 5 minutes","step_12":"Remove from heat and let rest for 15-20 minutes (borscht tastes better after resting)","step_13":"Serve hot with a generous dollop of sour cream and fresh dill","step_14":"Traditional accompaniments: pampushky (garlic bread rolls) and chopped raw bacon (salo)"}
