Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer for 25 minutes until vegetables are tender","step_6":"While soup simmers, make pistou: blend basil, garlic, and olive oil into a paste","step_7":"Stir Parmesan into pistou if using","step_8":"Season soup with salt and pepper","step_9":"Just before serving, stir in pistou","step_10":"Serve hot with crusty bread"}
{"_id":"be8d10ed-c595-485a-9c6e-873467997096","number":134,"title":"SPINACH AND RICOTTA QUICHE","cuisine":"French","meal_type":"Main Course/Breakfast","preparation_difficulty":"Medium","preparation_time":"1 hour","servings":"6","image_source":"","source":"French quiche adaptation","validation":"USDA - spinach provides iron (6.4mg/cup cooked), folate (263mcg), vitamin A; ricotta provides calcium","confidence":"Supported","tag_1":"menstrual-phase-week-1","tag_2":"fertility-supporting","tag_3":"pregnancy-month-4-6","tag_4":"vegetarian","tag_5":"contains-dairy","tag_6":"contains-eggs","tag_7":"calcium","tag_8":"calcium-rich","tag_9":"iron","tag_10":"iron-rich","tag_11":"folate","tag_12":"protein","tag_13":"protein-rich","tag_14":"NONE","tag_15":"NONE","principal_ingredient_1":"Spinach","principal_ingredient_2":"ricotta cheese","principal_ingredient_3":"eggs","principal_ingredient_4":"heavy cream","principal_ingredient_5":"pastry crust","principal_ingredient_6":null,"principal_ingredient_7":null,"subtitle":"Quiche aux Épinards et Ricotta","freeRecipe":false,"ingredient_1":"1 pre-made pie crust (or homemade shortcrust)","ingredient_2":"300g fresh spinach (or 250g frozen, thawed and squeezed)","ingredient_3":"250g whole milk ricotta cheese","ingredient_4":"3 large eggs","ingredient_5":"1/2 cup heavy cream or crème fraîche","ingredient_6":"1/2 cup grated Gruyère or Parmesan cheese","ingredient_7":"1/4 cup fresh dill or parsley, chopped","ingredient_8":"Pinch of nutmeg","ingredient_9":"Salt and pepper to taste","step_1":"Preheat oven to 180°C (350°F)","step_2":"Blind bake pie crust for 10 minutes: line with parchment, fill with pie weights, bake","step_3":"If using fresh spinach, wilt in a hot pan for 2 minutes, then squeeze out excess water and chop","step_4":"In a bowl, whisk eggs with ricotta and heavy cream","step_5":"Add chopped spinach, grated cheese, dill, nutmeg, salt, and pepper","step_6":"Pour filling into pre-baked crust","step_7":"Bake for 35-40 minutes until set and golden on top","step_8":"Let cool for 10 minutes before slicing","step_9":"Serve warm or at room temperature"}
